{"id": "EUVD-2026-86111", "enisaUuid": "ee8befa8-b7be-309b-9a10-e2adc8e33bb8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: chips-media: wave5: Release m2m_ctx after Instance Removed from List\n\nPossible use after free if IRQ thread manages to obtain spinlock between\nm2m_ctx release and wave5_release function removing stream instance from\nlist of active instances. The IRQ thread looks for the m2m_ctx which is\nfreed so null pointer dereference occurs.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:05:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:59", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e6bdd437a3c7a5d8846d7f58fe9645a60ec0933", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/04cda0b5c4ca3f61cbc86e41ead3c462c8cfd659", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7cdbd7bb21949a8fda10c7104a2b12ee363cbf5c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97513", "GHSA-rvcg-65g6-42r4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3be7b07a-0486-31f3-8bc9-607bd4ad39fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "3d490e8f-51ed-38ba-9787-fc9e24ab16af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "4ddcd711-b233-34a3-b650-cf8814b82987", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "53c5cb5f-5053-3d5d-98c1-be9f8f17b0e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9707a6254a8a6b978bde811a44fe07d86c229d1c <0e6bdd437a3c7a5d8846d7f58fe9645a60ec0933"}, {"id": "54ab167f-78e7-36ec-a243-b78c03a4161e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "5a6d9399-f632-3f61-a4ca-e2013f9ac557", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "b0fc6213-881a-328b-8cee-8627